# The findings the developer keeps, which the gauge leaves out. Each line names a file, or * for any file, then text
# the finding's line holds, then text the finding's message holds, apart by tabs. The comment above each says why.

# rec is the name of a parameter or a field, which Grazie reads as Redis misspelled.
internal/kiln/monitor_show.go	rec	Redis
internal/kiln/stats.go	rec	Redis

# A doc comment starts with the name it documents, which Grazie reads as a word.
internal/crash/flows_test.go	// due is	'do'
internal/kiln/hold.go	// due is	'do'
internal/kiln/monitor.go	// settings is	'are'
internal/tui/markdown.go	// markdown draws	formatting language
internal/tui/theme.go	// you marks	agreement

# a is the name of the receiver, which Grazie reads as an article.
internal/kiln/agent.go	into a,	Articles like 'a'

# go, python and typescript are the presets kiln init --preset takes by name.
internal/kiln/kiln.go	go, python and typescript	TypeScript

# A go:embed directive lists paths, not words.
*	//go:embed	repeated a word

# schemaOf fails the test on each reflect.Kind it has no schema for. Listing every other kind would add nothing.
internal/kiln/schema_test.go	switch typ.Kind()	Missing 'case'
